content.text:
Also media max-width override currently `.menu-footer { position: static; margin-top: 3vh; ... }` — override fine but now static duplicate; harmless. Need maybe menu button spacing/footer not overlap at short heights. We'll test.

Now ground rendering. Rewrite getSurfacePattern ground branch and drawPlatform ground branch. Let's implement a rich wet street.

Design cached pattern:
```
if (p.type === "ground") {
  const grad = ... top 0 #1b1e33, 0.1 #14162a, 0.35 #0e0f20, 1 #06050f
  fill.
  // curb strip 0..22
  g.fillStyle = "#1a1c2e"; fillRect(0,0,w,22)
  grad curb top lighter #2a2f4a
  // top bevel 0..3
  // curb seams vertical every 68
  // neon under-rail at y=20? maybe a thin emissive line
  // wet sheen over whole
  // reflections with lighter
  for each streak: x random, width 16-50; grad from y 22 to 22+height; color pick; alpha 0.06-0.12
  // puddle shapes at y ~30
  // road dashed lane line at y=84 with cyan/magenta faint
  // panel seams
  // grates/vents
  // specks
}
```
Palette unknown at cache creation? The cache key doesn't include palette, so we can't bake palette-specific colors except generic magenta/cyan. Fine. Could pass palette and key include glow? Better to bake neutral and overlay palette glow in drawPlatform. But streak colors can be magenta/cyan fixed since zone palettes alternate. Key by p.id-w only; that's okay.

Add reflection of top trim via additive.

drawPlatform ground:
```
const pal = palette;
ctx.drawImage(pattern,...)
// ambient bloom above surface
const bloom = ctx.createLinearGradient(0,p.y-18,0,p.y+22)
bloom.addColorStop(0, transparent), 0.55 glow 0.18, 1 transparent?
fillRect
// wet highlight line at p.y+3
// neon trim top: gradient horizontal? use glow
// moving scan/holo dash? maybe animated light sweep along surface
const sweep = ((time*90)%(p.w+400))-200
draw small gradient highlight at p.y+2, masked within p.w
// edge caps as before but nicer
```
Animated sweep could look great. Use ctx.save clip rect p.x..p.y+30; draw linear gradient of width 180 at x sweep with alpha 0.10 white-cyan.

Curb bevel: pattern has it.

Also platform floating improvement later maybe.

Let's edit.

